    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "What happens if you use the cosine rule in a right-angled triangle to find the length of the hypotenuse?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "It reduces to Pythagoras’ theorem, since $\\cos90^\\circ=0$.",
      "worked": "Let $c$ be the hypotenuse and $a,b$ the other sides.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}c^2&=a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos90^\\circ\\\\c^2&=a^2+b^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $\\cos90^\\circ=0$, this is Pythagoras’ theorem.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
